{"author":{"id":"a51b5961cc6de343a64125d8eb6a0f965aa434020b9c46ed932a1bbf143eb532"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791594519,"nonce":"/+Wa9iIROK92sDve9GuSDDr1Vuc=","title":"Remaining paint: clip-path, overflow-fade, backdrop-filter, text-decoration, text-align, url() backgrounds","message":"The CSS paint router (see the issue titled \"Land the blinc_abi css-paint branch\") covers backgrounds, borders, outlines, shadows, transform, filter, mask-image and corner shape. These parse, or are not known, and have no effect (checked for the first three with an offscreen probe).\n\n- clip-path: circle, ellipse, inset, rect, polygon and path(). RenderProps has clip_path; the type is blinc_layout's.\n- overflow-fade: RenderProps has overflow_fade, one distance per side.\n- backdrop-filter: blur and colour filters of what is behind a box; glass and backdrop filters live in side tables in blinc_abi, not RenderProps.\n- text-decoration (underlined links), text-align on wrapped text, text-overflow and line-clamp: none exist in either project, so they need the engine and the renderer.\n- background: url(): reported as unsupported today. Needs an image slot per source and fit (cover, contain, fill, tile); the renderer's image shader has the tile branch.\n- transition and animation: tracked in 35f7bd0.\n\nReference, for value coverage: ashui's haxe/ashui/css/Properties.hx, types/ClipPath.hx and ClipPathCss.hx.\n\nAcceptance, each: parsed in Rust with a unit test and the error text for a bad value; applied by the addon; an offscreen pixel test.","files":null}]}